!! Q: How do I make a team stand for its persons?

Set `kind.group-of: members` on the team type (its `members` field is a multi ref to person). A multi field that takes persons but not teams now also offers teams; picking or dropping one adds its members. If a field should keep the team itself, add `team` to its `ref-types`.

!! Q: How do I quick-create meetings from a jour fixe?

Set `kind.spawns: conversation` on the jour-fixe type (the conversation kind needs a `parent` ref that takes jour fixes; use `conversation:<field>` for another link field). Each jour fixe then shows ''＋ Meeting''. Fields both kinds have are copied; give the jour fixe's `participants` the team itself and each new meeting gets the team's current members. Give a field a `default` on the conversation kind (e.g. caption `[get[parent]get[caption]] [<now YYYY-0MM-0DD>] +[join[ ]]`) where it should be computed instead of copied.

!! Q: Can focus open more than the children?

Yes. Create the kind's rules tiddler (type-builder: ''＋ rules'' next to the focus checkbox) and add one filter per line; `<host>` is the focused instance. For a person:

```
# the tiddlers whose parent is the person
[function[kind.focus-parent],<host>]
# topics where the person is stakeholder, status empty or active
[kind.type[topic]contains:stakeholder<host>] :filter[get[status]else[active]match[active]]
# notes that inform the person
[kind.type[note]contains:inform<host>]
```

The story then shows the person, the children, the open topics and the notes, in that order, each group latest first.

!! Q: How do I hide archived instances in pickers?

Put a filter into `$:/config/rimir/kind/instance-filter` (Settings → ''Instance filter''), e.g. `[!status[archived]]`. kind runs it on the candidate list of every ref picker (editor/creator/graph-modal dropdown, group candidates, palette ref lists, wizard pickers, rimir/ports), so an archived topic is no longer offered. Status values stay your model's business: kind only applies the filter.

`$:/config/rimir/kind/instance-filter/apply-to` names where it applies: `pickers` (shipped), `cockpit` (incoming rows of the generic cockpit), `overview` (Instances Overview nodes). Values already linked are never hidden: the field bar, the editor pills and the outgoing cockpit sections show them, and the palette toggle lists keep them so they can be unlinked.

To also hide what sits below an archived instance, write a `$:/tags/Global` function and call it from the filter. One level (the instance or its `parent` archived):

```
\function my.live() [!status[archived]] :filter[get[parent]status[archived]count[]match[0]]
```

with `[my.live[]]` as the instance filter; for deeper trees make the function walk up the `parent` chain. Globals are in scope wherever the page template renders (story, graph modal, overview). The cascade palette imports only `$:/tags/Macro` tiddlers, so there a Global function is not found; tag the function tiddler `$:/tags/Macro` as well if you use the palette pickers.

!! Q: How do I hide the cockpit or give a kind its own one?

Set `kind.cockpit` on the type tiddler. `none` hides the panel for that kind. Any other value is the title of a tiddler that is shown instead of the generic panel, with `currentTiddler` (and `<<host>>`) set to the instance; it can `\import $:/plugins/rimir/kind/engine` and reuse `kind.iview-click-toggle`, `kind.iview-link`, `kind.iview-detail` and `kind.instance-content`. Cockpits that depend on one data model (fixed field names, status values, kind ranking) belong with that model, not in kind.
